        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): actively schedule launchd relaunch on supervisor restart",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n#104538 (P0): on a macOS launchd-managed install, a gateway-tool/SIGUSR1 restart takes the \"full process restart (supervisor restart)\" path — the gateway writes its handoff, pauses briefly, and **exits, trusting launchd `KeepAlive` to relaunch it**. In launchd domains where KeepAlive never fires (verified by the reporter: killing the gateway never respawns it, and a fresh test LaunchAgent behaves the same), routine config-change restarts leave the gateway dead until a manual `launchctl kickstart`. The same installs have a *working* restart path (`source=launchd-handoff mode=kickstart` in `gateway-restart.log`) — it just wasn't used for SIGUSR1 restarts.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPer the triage's best solution (\"route launchd-detected routine restarts through the existing detached launchctl handoff … and fall back to an in-process restart if handoff scheduling fails\"):\n\n- `restartGatewayProcessWithFreshPid` now schedules `scheduleDetachedLaunchdRestartHandoff({ mode: \"kickstart\", waitForPid: process.pid })` for launchd-detected restarts before returning `supervised`. The detached helper **waits for this exact pid to exit** — restart timing stays sequenced by the real process exit, addressing the prior comment's concern about a second helper racing launchd — then re-enables the service and kickstarts with a bootstrap fallback; **launchd still performs the relaunch itself**.\n- If the handoff cannot be scheduled, the function returns `failed`, which the run-loop already maps to the in-process restart fallback — the gateway never exits into a domain with no scheduled relaunch.\n- Windows `schtasks` already had this active-scheduling shape (`triggerOpenClawRestart`); launchd now matches it.\n\n## User Impact\n\nlaunchd installs whose KeepAlive is inert (the reported domain state) no longer lose the gateway on ordinary config-change restarts; installs with healthy KeepAlive see no behavior change beyond the handoff also firing (kickstart of an already-relaunched service is a no-op).\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Live before/after on a real macOS LaunchAgent** (this machine, macOS 25.x; throwaway agent `ai.openclaw.test104538` with **`KeepAlive=false`** to reproduce the broken-domain condition, fresh `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`, agent booted via `launchctl bootstrap` + `kickstart`):\n\n| | old pid | SIGUSR1 → | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| current `main` dist | 91768 (http 200) | exits | **`pid=none`, http 000 — dead until manual kickstart** (the reported behavior) |\n| this PR's dist | 90843 (http 200) | exits → handoff fires | **new pid 91120, http 200** |\n\n`gateway-restart.log` from the after-fix run — the exact signature of the issue's known-working path, now emitted by a SIGUSR1 restart:\n```\n[2026-07-11T18:55:38Z] openclaw restart attempt source=launchd-handoff mode=kickstart target=gui/501/ai.openclaw.test104538 waitPid=90843\n[2026-07-11T18:55:40Z] openclaw restart done    source=launchd-handoff mode=kickstart\n```\n\n**Regressions** (`process-respawn.test.ts`, 27 tests): launchd restarts schedule the kickstart handoff with `waitForPid: process.pid` across all three detection paths (marker env, `LAUNCH_JOB_LABEL`, `XPC_SERVICE_NAME`); scheduling failure returns `failed` (in-process fallback). **Fails on prior head**: 5 launchd tests fail (no handoff scheduled, no failure fallback). `run-loop.test.ts` 42-total suite green; `tsgo:core` 0; oxlint/oxfmt clean. Throwaway LaunchAgent booted out and removed after the proof.\n\nFixes #104538\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01AJogTw4aGDiacwqju1uod6\n",
        "branch": "fix/launchd-restart-active-kickstart-104538",
